# Build context is ./backend. Everything here either bloats the image, breaks
# reproducibility, or leaks host state into the container.
#
# Note on patterns: .dockerignore matches with Go's filepath.Match, which does
# NOT recurse. "__pycache__/" matches only a __pycache__ directory at the root
# of the context — nested ones are still copied. Anything that can appear at any
# depth therefore needs an explicit "**/" prefix. Patterns deliberately left
# without one are anchored to the context root because a recursive version would
# match real source (see storage/ below).

# Host virtualenv — Windows-built, cp314 Windows wheels, ~5GB with torch.
# Copying it in would shadow /opt/venv's Linux packages.
.venv/
venv/
env/
**/.venv/

# Bytecode compiled against the host interpreter/platform. These MUST be
# excluded at every depth: CPython will happily load a cached .pyc whose source
# mtime and size still match, so a Windows-built cache shipped into the image
# gets executed in place of the code that was copied in — which surfaces as
# tracebacks citing C:\ paths from inside the container.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*$py.class
**/*.so

# Test and lint caches.
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/htmlcov/
**/.coverage

# Uploaded documents live in a named volume, never in the image. Baking the
# host's uploads in would ship real documents to every environment.
#
# Root-anchored on purpose: app/core/storage/ is application source, and a
# recursive "**/storage/" would silently drop it and break the build.
storage/

# Secrets. Config comes from the environment (compose env_file), and an .env
# copied into the image would silently win over it for anything unset.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Scratch output from local runs.
uvicorn_err.txt
uvicorn_out.txt
**/*.log

# Editor/OS noise.
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/*.swp
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
